  "fact_notes": [
    "架空の教材例・思考実験。実在の調査、統計、制度、実証結果ではない。登録台帳は制作来歴確認用。"
  ],
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "id": "p1",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "On Friday afternoon, four friends boarded a crowded bus after their school sports festival.",
          "ja": "金曜の午後、四人の友人は体育祭の後、混んだバスに乗った。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Only one seat remained empty, and everyone was exhausted from the day's activities.",
          "ja": "空席は一つだけで、全員が一日の活動で疲れ切っていた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Ken offered the seat to Emi, who immediately refused because she thought that he looked more tired than she did.",
          "ja": "ケンはエミに席を譲ったが、彼の方が疲れて見えたため彼女はすぐ断った。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Neither sat down until another passenger took the seat.",
          "ja": "別の乗客が座るまで二人とも座らなかった。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p2",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Later, Ken complained that Emi had rejected his kindness.",
          "ja": "後でケンはエミが自分の親切を拒んだと不満を言った。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Emi was surprised because she had actually intended to return the favor.",
          "ja": "エミは実際には親切に報いるつもりだったので驚いた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Their friend Yuta suggested that each had interpreted the other's behavior differently.",
          "ja": "友人のユウタは互いの行動を違って解釈したのだと提案した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They realized that both had tried to be considerate, yet neither had understood the other's intention.",
          "ja": "二人とも思いやろうとしたが相手の意図を理解していなかったと気づいた。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p3",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "The following week, the friends discussed how to avoid similar misunderstandings.",
          "ja": "翌週、友人たちは同様の誤解を避ける方法を話し合った。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Instead of refusing an offer automatically, they decided to explain their reasons briefly.",
          "ja": "申し出を自動的に断る代わりに理由を短く説明することにした。"
        },
        {
          "en": "They also agreed that accepting assistance need not indicate weakness or a lack of gratitude.",
          "ja": "援助を受け入れても弱さや感謝の欠如を意味する必要はないと合意した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "A simple expression of thanks could communicate appreciation without requiring an immediate exchange.",
          "ja": "簡単な感謝の言葉で即時の見返りを求めず感謝を伝えられる。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p4",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "On another crowded bus, Ken asked whether Emi actually wanted the available seat.",
          "ja": "別の混んだバスでケンはエミが本当に空席に座りたいか尋ねた。"
        },
        {
          "en": "She accepted the offer and explained that her ankle was sore after practice.",
          "ja": "エミは申し出を受け入れ練習後に足首が痛むと説明した。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Ken discovered that asking a question could be more helpful than relying on his own assumptions.",
          "ja": "自分の思い込みに頼るより尋ねる方が役立つとケンは知った。"
        },
        {
          "en": "Their conversation was short, but it made the situation less awkward for everyone.",
          "ja": "会話は短かったが全員にとって気まずさが減った。"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "p5",
      "sentences": [
        {
          "en": "Kindness involves more than attempting to do what seems appropriate.",
          "ja": "親切には適切に見えることを行おうとする以上のことが含まれる。"
        },
        {
          "en": "It also involves recognizing that another person's preferences may differ from one's expectations.",
          "ja": "他者の好みが自分の期待と異なり得ることを認識することも含む。"
        },
        {
          "en": "People cannot always predict how their actions will be understood.",
          "ja": "人は自分の行動の受け取られ方を常に予測できるわけではない。"
        },
        {
          "en": "The friends learned that honest communication can help good intentions become meaningful support.",
          "ja": "友人たちは率直な意思疎通によって善意が意味のある支援になり得ると学んだ。"
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
